  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "A hungry fly speeds through a forest."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "It smells nectar and lands on a green leaf."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "It starts to drink the sweet liquid."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "Suddenly, the fly’s world turns green."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "The two sides of the leaf close against each other."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Long green teeth lock together around it."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "The fly has been caught by a Venus flytrap."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "There is no escape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "The Venus flytrap is perhaps the most famous killer plant."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "However, scientists have only recently started to understand how it hunts and eats."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "After years of study, plant scientist Alexander Volkov believes he now knows the Venus flytrap’s secret."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "“This,” says Volkov, “is an electrical plant.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "There are three small hairs along each of the Venus flytrap’s two leaves."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "When an insect touches a hair, it creates an electrical signal in the leaf."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "The insect can continue feeding—for now."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "But if it touches another hair within 20 seconds, the trap snaps shut."
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "This system allows the plant to tell the difference between a drop of water, for example, and a moving creature."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "Once trapped, an insect has little chance of survival."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "Instead of nectar, the Venus flytrap now releases a different liquid—one that slowly eats away at the insect."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "Ten days later, almost nothing is left."
          },
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "The plant’s leaves open again, and the Venus flytrap is ready for its next meal."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
